Skill: skill patch of the dev-env repository, https://github.com/jeonghanlee/dev-env
  (a copy of the file, taken from a clean checkout; no line was added)
Needs: bash and patch
Use: the revert_patch_src macro of configure/RULES_FUNC calls
  bash scripts/revert_patch.bash --no-backup-if-mismatch <source> <patch>
Exit status of the tool: 0 reversed or already unapplied, 1 patch failed while
  reversing, 2 usage or input error, 3 the state cannot be classified. make
  reports a failing rule as exit status 2.
Limit stated in the skill: for a single-file, single-hunk patch of a static C
  function that changes only the last body line, a second revert on an unapplied
  state is not safe. The patch of this repository adds one line to CMakeLists.txt
  and is not such a patch.
